/// The standard kinds and currencies that almost every ledger reaches for.
///
/// Place kinds say what an account is (a bank, a broker, a loan) and carry the
/// rules that follow from it. Commodity kinds say what a unit is (a currency, a
/// stock, a house). Entity kinds say who someone is (a person, an employer, a
/// grant).
///
/// Currency precision follows ISO 4217. Like every system, this is
/// community-maintained data: check a figure against its official source
/// before relying on it, and send a fix when it is wrong.
system std


// ─── Places: assets ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Physical cash and money held outside any institution.
kind cash : asset

/// A checking, savings or money-market account.
kind bank : asset
  /// A bank balance below zero is an overdraft: the bank is lending you the
  /// difference, usually for a fee.
  ///
  /// To fix: move money in before the payment clears, or look for a pending
  /// payment or a missing deposit that explains it.
  law overdraft
    always
    warn balance >= empty "balance below zero"

/// A brokerage account. Sales relieve the oldest shares first, unless a
/// selector or the account says otherwise.
kind broker : asset
  select fifo

/// Land, a house or a share of one: a home, or a rental.
kind property : asset

/// Things kept for your own use rather than for profit. A gain on one is
/// income; a loss on one is not a deduction.
kind personal-use : asset

/// A car, a boat, anything with a title.
kind vehicle : personal-use

/// Money owed to you: an invoice you sent, a loan to a friend, a deposit you
/// paid. A flow into it that says `due` is one claim, kept apart from the
/// others, and a flow `for` its `#code` settles it. What it holds is coming
/// in, never money to spend.
kind receivable : asset
  claim

/// Money a servicer holds for you to pay taxes and insurance on your home. It
/// is yours and it is not spendable: it leaves only by paying those bills.
kind escrow : asset
  liquidity 365d


// ─── Places: liabilities ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Revolving credit. Spending goes in, payments come out of a bank account.
kind credit-card : liability

/// Money you owe on a bill: what a flow out of it (the bill) says is due, and
/// what a flow into it (the payment) settles, `for` the bill's `#code`.
kind payable : liability
  claim

/// Money borrowed for a term.
kind loan : liability
  has rate     percent
  has maturity date

  /// A loan is repaid in full by its maturity date. The journal has reached
  /// that date with a balance still owed.
  ///
  /// To fix: record the missing payments, or, if the term was extended, update
  /// `maturity` on the account.
  law payoff
    by self.maturity
    require self.balance == empty "balance still owed at maturity"

/// A loan secured by a home.
kind mortgage : loan


// ─── Places: income ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Pay for work. Tax systems count what arrives from a place of this kind.
kind wages : income

/// Interest earned.
kind interest : income

/// Dividends earned.
kind dividends : income

/// Profit from selling something for more than it cost.
kind gains : income


// ─── Places: expenses ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Tuition, books and fees. A 529 plan and a grant for education spend here.
kind education : expense

/// Doctors, prescriptions and insurance costs. An HSA spends here.
kind medical : expense


// ─── Commodities ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Legal tender.
kind currency : commodity

/// Anything traded on a market.
kind security : commodity

/// A share of a company.
kind stock : security
  liquidity 1d

/// A pooled fund: a mutual fund or an ETF.
kind fund : security
  liquidity 2d

/// A loan you hold, or a note that pays interest.
kind bond : security
  liquidity 2d

/// A digital asset.
kind crypto : commodity
  liquidity 1d

/// Land and buildings, counted in units you choose (one house, one acre).
kind real-estate : commodity
  liquidity 90d

/// A thing you own that is not money: a car, a painting, a bag of gold.
kind good : commodity
  liquidity 30d


// ─── Entities ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

/// Someone whose tax is figured, alone or together. `filing` says how, and
/// `children` is how many qualifying children there are to claim.
kind taxpayer : entity
  has filing   name
  has children number
  children     0

/// A human being. Alone, a person files as `single` unless they say otherwise.
kind person : taxpayer
  has born date
  filing single

/// People who share money and file one return: its members `member` it. It
/// owns what they hold together, lives where they live, and is governed as one,
/// so its members' pay counts into one return, and it files `joint`. What is
/// personal stays with the person: a 401(k)'s yearly limit, the age that opens
/// a withdrawal.
kind household : taxpayer
  filing joint

/// Anyone who is not a person: a company, a school, a landlord.
kind org : entity

/// Someone who pays you for work.
kind employer : org

/// A body that governs and taxes.
kind government : org

/// Money you set aside for something: an emergency fund, a trip, a tax
/// vault. A flow that says `for` it ties what arrives to it. That money is not
/// available to spend, and spending it is a flow `for` you again, or a payment
/// straight out of the envelope.
kind envelope : entity
  restricted

/// Money given for a stated purpose, until a stated day. Money from a grant
/// stays tied to it after it lands in your account, and may only be spent on
/// what the grant names.
kind grant : entity
  restricted
  has purpose kind
  has until  date

  /// Grant money may only be spent on what the grant names. This payment went
  /// somewhere else.
  ///
  /// To fix: pay it from another account, or, if the funder agreed to the
  /// change, update `purpose` on the grant.
  law purpose
    on spend
    require to is self.purpose "grant money spent outside its purpose"

  /// A grant ends on its `until` date, and unspent money is owed back.
  ///
  /// To fix: spend what is left on the grant's purpose before the deadline, or
  /// ask the funder for an extension and move `until`.
  law deadline
    by self.until
    require remaining == empty "grant money left unspent at the deadline"


// ─── Currencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

commodity USD : currency
  name "United States dollar"
  precision 2

commodity EUR : currency
  name "Euro"
  precision 2

commodity GBP : currency
  name "Pound sterling"
  precision 2

commodity CAD : currency
  name "Canadian dollar"
  precision 2

commodity AUD : currency
  name "Australian dollar"
  precision 2

commodity NZD : currency
  name "New Zealand dollar"
  precision 2

commodity CHF : currency
  name "Swiss franc"
  precision 2

commodity SEK : currency
  name "Swedish krona"
  precision 2

commodity NOK : currency
  name "Norwegian krone"
  precision 2

commodity DKK : currency
  name "Danish krone"
  precision 2

commodity PLN : currency
  name "Polish zloty"
  precision 2

commodity CNY : currency
  name "Chinese yuan"
  precision 2

commodity HKD : currency
  name "Hong Kong dollar"
  precision 2

commodity SGD : currency
  name "Singapore dollar"
  precision 2

commodity INR : currency
  name "Indian rupee"
  precision 2

commodity MXN : currency
  name "Mexican peso"
  precision 2

commodity BRL : currency
  name "Brazilian real"
  precision 2

commodity ZAR : currency
  name "South African rand"
  precision 2

commodity JPY : currency
  name "Japanese yen"
  precision 0

commodity KRW : currency
  name "South Korean won"
  precision 0

commodity VND : currency
  name "Vietnamese dong"
  precision 0

commodity ISK : currency
  name "Icelandic krona"
  precision 0

commodity BHD : currency
  name "Bahraini dinar"
  precision 3

commodity KWD : currency
  name "Kuwaiti dinar"
  precision 3

commodity OMR : currency
  name "Omani rial"
  precision 3

commodity JOD : currency
  name "Jordanian dinar"
  precision 3
